From 4b852c79804e4f4ea1d1f89889e45f78902537bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?L=C6=B0u=20Oa=20Oa?=
 <212658678+luuoaoa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 03:09:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Vietnamese IME: add a "restore non-Vietnamese words"
 Telex/VNI option
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The vendored UniKey engine already restores the original keystrokes when a typed
word is not valid Vietnamese (so "worldcup" stays "worldcup" instead of becoming
"wỏldcup"), but it was hardcoded on in unikey_engine.cc:

  mem_->options.spellCheckEnabled = 1;   // detects the invalid word
  mem_->options.autoNonVnRestore = 1;    // restores the keystrokes

Expose it as a user-visible toggle, plumbed live on the same focus /
options-changed seam as the other Telex settings (telex-settings-0001):

- input_method.mojom: new enable_restore_non_vietnamese_words field on both
  VietnameseTelexSettings (@5) and VietnameseVniSettings (@4), MinVersion=26.
- input_method_settings.cc/.h: new pref keys
  vietnameseTelexEnableNonVnRestore / vietnameseVniEnableNonVnRestore, read into
  the settings union (default ON) with matching UMA.
- unikey_engine.cc ApplySettings: drive spellCheckEnabled + autoNonVnRestore
  from the pref (was hardcoded 1); default on so mixed English/Vietnamese typing
  "just works".
- os-settings front end (input_method_util.ts, prefs_consts/defaults.ts,
  options_page.ts): new VIETNAMESE_*_ENABLE_NON_VN_RESTORE toggle in its own
  section of the Telex and VNI options pages, default on.
- os_settings_strings.grdp + inputs_section.cc: label "Restore non-Vietnamese
  words" and its description.

Default: ON. Chosen so a user typing mixed English/Vietnamese gets English words
left intact without touching settings; turning it off makes the engine always
apply Vietnamese diacritics.

Scope note: the UnikeyEngine only serves Telex (kTelexSpec == "m17n:vi_telex");
VNI is served by the rule-based engine, which discards runtime settings. The VNI
toggle is added for parity and flows through the mojom union, but is currently
inert on the VNI path — exactly like the pre-existing VNI toggles.

